With a Tonga dGPU installed in a Raven1 system I see (attached) dmesg 
warning from init.

Also, every warm reboot results in my Tonga failing to init (also 
attached).  If I cold reboot (hit the reset button) it works fine.

Note I get the DCN message regardless if I warm or cold reboot.


commit d35c9287c92f330f07b3e87f7f2953b1c822c8e3 (HEAD, refs/bisect/bad)
Author: Mikita Lipski <mikita.lipski-5C7GfCeVMHo@public.gmane.org>
Date:   Thu May 31 14:49:00 2018 -0400

     drm/amd/display: Enable PPLib calls from DC on linux

     Set the powerplay debug flag to false for both Windows and Linux
     to allow the calls to pplib. So we can retrieve the clock values
     from powerplay instead of using default hardcoded values.

     Signed-off-by: Mikita Lipski <mikita.lipski-5C7GfCeVMHo@public.gmane.org>
